---
description: Clean code test rules for writing readable, fast, independent, and repeatable tests
globs: "**/tests/**/*.php"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Clean Code: Tests

## One assert per test (one concept per test)

```php
// BAD
public function testUser(): void
{
    $user = User::factory()->create();
    $this->assertNotNull($user->id);
    $this->assertEquals('active', $user->status);
    $this->assertTrue($user->hasRole('member'));
}

// GOOD
public function testUserIsCreatedWithId(): void
{
    $user = User::factory()->create();
    $this->assertNotNull($user->id);
}

public function testNewUserHasActiveStatus(): void
{
    $user = User::factory()->create();
    $this->assertEquals('active', $user->status);
}
```

## Tests must be readable - descriptive names and clear setup

```php
// BAD
public function testIt(): void
{
    $u = User::factory()->create(['r' => 'a']);
    $this->actingAs($u)->get('/d')->assertOk();
}

// GOOD
public function testAdminCanAccessDashboard(): void
{
    $admin = User::factory()->admin()->create();
    $this->actingAs($admin)->get('/dashboard')->assertOk();
}
```

## Tests must be fast - mock external dependencies

```php
// BAD - hits real external API
public function testPayment(): void
{
    $result = (new StripeGateway())->charge(1000);
    $this->assertTrue($result->success);
}

// GOOD
public function testPaymentChargesSuccessfully(): void
{
    $this->mock(PaymentGateway::class)
        ->shouldReceive('charge')->once()->andReturn(new PaymentResult(success: true));
}
```

## Tests must be independent - no shared mutable state

```php
// BAD - depends on other test's state
public function testCreateOrder(): void { $this->orderId = Order::factory()->create()->id; }
public function testCancelOrder(): void { Order::find($this->orderId)->cancel(); }

// GOOD
public function testCancelOrder(): void
{
    $order = Order::factory()->create();
    $order->cancel();
    $this->assertEquals('cancelled', $order->fresh()->status);
}
```

## Tests must be repeatable - same result every run

```php
// BAD - depends on real time
public function testDiscount(): void
{
    $this->assertTrue($product->hasDiscount());
}

// GOOD - freeze time
public function testDiscountActiveDuringPromo(): void
{
    $this->travelTo(Carbon::parse('2026-01-15'));
    $product = Product::factory()->withPromo()->create();
    $this->assertTrue($product->hasDiscount());
}
```
